The Art-Deco-Interactive-Showcase's `animate()` called `requestAnimationFrame(animate)` unconditionally on every frame — running at 60fps indefinitely even when auto-rotation was disabled and nothing was changing.

## Changes

- **New `src/components/ArtDecoShowcase.tsx`** — React port of the Art Deco Pyramid Jewelry Box viewer with the loop fixed:
  - `startLoop()` guards on `!autoRotateRef.current` and the inner loop self-terminates when auto-rotate is toggled off
  - User interactions (drag, scroll-to-zoom, tier selection) use a single on-demand `requestAnimationFrame` via `requestRedraw()` — no persistent loop when idle
- **`App.tsx`** — adds "Art Deco Showcase" as a fourth NEXUS portfolio tab alongside Neural Forge, Algorithm Arena, and Systems Pulse
- **`App.test.tsx`** — adds `closePath` to the canvas mock; adds a tab-switching test for the new component
- **`package.json`** — moves `@testing-library/dom` from `dependencies` → `devDependencies`
- **`vite.config.ts`** — fixes pre-existing `manualChunks` object→function for Vite 8 compatibility; path matching uses trailing slashes to avoid false matches on similarly-named packages

```ts
// Before: loop runs forever regardless of state
function animate() {
  if (autoRotateEnabled) rotation.y += 0.01;
  drawPyramid();
  requestAnimationFrame(animate); // unconditional
}

// After: loop only lives while auto-rotate is on
const startLoop = () => {
  if (animIdRef.current !== 0 || !autoRotateRef.current) return;
  const loop = () => {
    if (autoRotateRef.current) {
      rotationRef.current.y += 0.01;
      drawFrame();
      animIdRef.current = requestAnimationFrame(loop);
    } else {
      animIdRef.current = 0; // self-terminates
    }
  };
  animIdRef.current = requestAnimationFrame(loop);
};
```

The shared Hugging Face free-tier deployment can exhaust storage/inference quota under heavy signup traffic. This change adds explicit self-hosting guidance and introduces signup-time prompts on the official hosted URL to encourage forked deployments before creating new accounts.

- **Docs: Free self-hosting path + sync workflow**
  - Added a new README section: **Host your own instance (free on Hugging Face)**.
  - Documents fork → Hugging Face Space creation via **Docker SDK** → deploy.
  - Added fork maintenance guidance: **Sync fork** + automatic Space rebuild behavior.

- **Auth UX: official-instance-specific signup friction**
  - Added origin detection for the official host (`https://coryconway-theowrestle.hf.space`).
  - In register mode on the official host, shows a capacity notice encouraging users to host their own fork.
  - Replaced `window.confirm` with an accessible 2-step `AlertDialog` flow (official host only):
    1. “Could you host your own free instance first?”
    2. “Confirm before creating account” (can’t self-host right now)

- **Implementation details**
  - Added `src/lib/hosting.ts`:
    ```ts
    export const OFFICIAL_HOST_ORIGIN = "https://coryconway-theowrestle.hf.space";

    export function isOfficialHostedInstance(url: string): boolean {
      try {
        return new URL(url).origin === OFFICIAL_HOST_ORIGIN;
      } catch {
        return false;
      }
    }
    ```
  - `AuthPage` now gates register submission through the dialog flow when `isOfficialHostedInstance(...)` is true.
  - Added focused unit tests in `src/tests/hosting.test.ts` (official origin, non-official origin, invalid URL, protocol mismatch).

