nginx 502s on the GitHub OAuth proxy locations when running on newer `nginx:alpine` (1.29.7). The upstream HTTPS connection to `github.com` fails before GitHub ever responds.

## Changes to `nginx.conf`

- **`resolver 127.0.0.11 valid=30s`** — wire up Docker's embedded DNS for runtime hostname resolution; without this, nginx resolves once at startup and caches indefinitely
- **`proxy_ssl_verify off`** — make SSL verification opt-out explicit; newer nginx mainline builds can behave more strictly than the documented default
- **`proxy_http_version 1.1`** — upstream connections default to HTTP/1.0; some newer servers return responses nginx rejects as invalid under 1.0, producing a 502

```nginx
location = /github-oauth/login/device/code {
    proxy_pass https://github.com/login/device/code;
    proxy_ssl_server_name on;
    proxy_ssl_verify off;
    proxy_http_version 1.1;
    ...
}
```
